.policy "ruff-ytt303-sys-version-slice1" revision 2
.description "Read the major version from sys.version_info instead of slicing the first character of sys.version; the first digit is wrong for a two-digit major version."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff YTT303 (flake8-2020): `sys.version[:1]`, the major version as one character. On Python 10 it is "1".
//   sys.version[:1]          ← YTT303
//   version[:1]              ← YTT303 after `from sys import version`
#include "python/misc2-version.rr"

.violation YTT303(at: node) code "YTT303"
    "Use `sys.version_info.major` (an int, so compare it to ints, not strings) instead of `sys.version[:1]`, which is only the first digit of a two-digit major version."
    suppress ruff "YTT303"
YTT303(v) :- ytt_version_upto(v, "1").
